WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.067
The breaking news.

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.535
Lawyers for former President

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.269
Donald Trump

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.704
have been seen going

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:07.007
into the Department of justice.

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:07.941
You write in the rember

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:08.875
that Trump's attorneys

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:09.976
requested a meeting

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:11.644
with Attorney General Merrick Garland

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:12.345
last month

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.013
in connection

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:14.948
with the special counsel's investigation

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:17.217
of classified documents at Mar a Lago.

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:18.151
CNN's Evan

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:19.619
Perez joins us now

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:22.322
with the very latest on what is going on.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.991
Evan, is this meeting still taking place?

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.261
It is still taking place,

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:29.596
as far as we can tell.

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:30.330
John,

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.632
we have not seen the Trump attorneys

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:33.666
leave the building.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:34.634
There's only one way

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:35.769
in and out for visitors.

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:37.404
So we're sitting there

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:39.239
waiting to see what they might say

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:40.340
when they when they exit.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:40.940
But, look,

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.710
this is a meeting that the Trump lawyers

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:46.379
requested just in

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.214
just a couple of weeks ago now.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.350
They were asking to meet

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.684
with the attorney general,

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:52.318
Merrick Garland.

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:53.319
No sign

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:54.287
that Merrick Garland

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:55.922
is actually meeting with them

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:57.090
at this moment.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:57.557
Neither.

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:58.892
Any sign that that

00:00:58.892 --> 00:00:59.659
that they're meeting

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.027
with the deputy attorney general,

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.762
Lisa Monaco,

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:03.830
the way these things work,

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.398
you know,
certainly for the Justice Department,

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.032
because they're trying

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.434
to keep this investigation

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:09.736
in the hands of

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:10.403
Jack Smith,

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.671
the special counsel

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.572
is, you know,

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.441
they might try to accommodate

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:14.941
a meeting

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.409
with somebody who is a career

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.211
official here at the Justice Department

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.412
who can at least hear

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.047
these complaints that they have.

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:21.781
What the Trump

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.850
attorneys wrote in their letter

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.251
is that they believe that there's

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.187
been prosecutorial misconduct

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:29.022
that has gone on in this investigation.

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:30.523
They didn't specify

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:31.558
what exactly

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:33.026
that prosecutorial misconduct,

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.727
just that the former president

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.262
is being treated like,

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.397
unlike anyone

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:39.499
in the history of the presidency.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.334
And so that's partly what they

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.302
their beef is

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:43.336
and that's what they want to try

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:46.172
to bring across in this meeting today.

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:47.173
Now, again,

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.342
we don't know the specifics of that

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:50.844
alleged misconduct

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:52.078
that they're making

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.179
that they're claiming.

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:54.380
But we do know that one of the things

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.782
they're very unhappy about

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.183
is the fact that Jack Smith

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.418
and the prosecutors

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.552
have obtained

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.855
a trove of information, including client

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:02.755
attorney client

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.157
privilege material, material

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:05.892
that normally is shielded

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.227
from investigator

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:08.061
But they got that

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:09.796
because a judge determined

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.197
that there was an exception

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.699
under the crime fraud

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:13.533
exception

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:15.101
that allows prosecutors

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.436
to obtain that kind of evidence.

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:18.838
So again, we don't know exactly what

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.407
how long this meeting is going to go,

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.743
who exactly they're meeting with.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.311
But we know that what they want

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:26.746
is they want to delay

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:27.981
some claims

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:28.681
about the way

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:30.750
this investigation has been ongoing John.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.317
And just have

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.919
one more question on the timing here,

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:34.254
because I know you and others

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:35.255
are reporting

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:37.624
that the grand jury that has been hearing

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.792
testimony about this is back

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.794
meeting again now

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.496
for the first time in some time.

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:44.397
So what does that tell you?

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:47.300
Right exactly?

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:47.901
I think

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.436
that the context, the crucial timing,

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.438
I think, is very important here.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:53.339
All signs

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.408
indicate that this is an investigation

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:57.477
in its closing stages.

00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:59.679
And that could mean a number of things.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:00.914
That could mean that

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:01.714
the grand jury,

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:04.284
which hasn't been seen at the courthouse

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:07.921
since early May, is coming back

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:10.056
to get some wrap up witnesses

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:11.925
to get some additional testimony.

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:12.659
It could be

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:14.327
that you bring back a grand jury

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:16.162
that hasn't met in weeks.

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:17.730
To bring an indictment.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.832
So there's a number of possibilities

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:21.467
that this grand jury

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.036
could be coming back for.

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.103
We do not know.

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:24.737
Obviously, Jack

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.439
Smith is holding his cards

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:27.874
very close to the vest.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.809
But I think that's one of the reasons

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:31.878
why this meeting is so important,

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:33.513
certainly from the Trump perspective,

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:34.781
because if they want to try

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:36.249
to get to somebody

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:38.351
inside this building to say

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:39.953
that there should be a pause,

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:40.386
that there should

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:41.854
something should be stopped,

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:44.157
now is the time to do that, John.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:44.791
All right,

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:45.425
Evan Perez,

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:47.360
we're gonna let you get back to reporting

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.228
if you learn anything new

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.262
about this meeting.

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:50.897
Get back to us right away.

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:52.198
In the meantime, we're going to speak

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:53.733
to CNN legal analyst Laura Coates.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:54.300
Counselor.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.969
Great to see you.

00:03:55.969 --> 00:03:58.304
First, a general question.

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:59.672
In a meeting like this,

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.007
which is not unheard of

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:02.575
when you have

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:04.177
someone who is being investigated

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:05.445
their attorneys asked to meet

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:06.279
with prosecutors,

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:07.947
what's the nature of the conversation

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:08.948
behind closed doors?

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:11.951
Well, first

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.086
of all, the power dynamic

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:14.988
you have to keep in mind here, John,

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:16.256
it's the prosecutors

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:18.424
who have all of the power here.

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:20.426
They know what testimony has come

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:21.728
in, what has not.

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:23.663
They know if there are any gaps

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:24.964
in their evidentiary burden

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:27.533
looking towards perhaps a prosecution.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.602
They know what witnesses there have been.

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:31.471
They know who is cooperating.

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:32.672
They know who is not.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:33.506
And they've largely

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:34.974
probably been able to outline

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:36.542
what are the potential statutes

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.411
that could be implicated by the conduct

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:39.812
that they are now investigating.

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:40.413
And so

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:42.582
when they hold the bulk of those cards,

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:43.483
this meeting is not

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:45.018
just a magnanimous gesture.

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:45.852
I don't want to make that

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:46.919
to make that claim.

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:48.221
But what it is, is somebody

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:51.090
who has the intention as the prosecutor

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:52.892
to be closed mouth,

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:54.661
to not be as forthcoming

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:55.862
as they could be.

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:57.063
Say if they were in an open

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:58.298
courtroom or trial,

00:04:58.298 --> 00:04:59.232
because the other side

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:00.500
is every incentive to then

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.835
go out and talk and try to spin.

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:04.470
And that has already been the track

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.338
record here.

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:06.973
The idea of misconduct

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:08.875
is a huge allegation,

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:10.176
a huge claim to level

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:11.611
against any prosecutor.

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:12.011
But certainly

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:13.546
the Department of Justice, obviously,

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:14.814
knowing that they have gone

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:16.649
to great lengths to Jack Smith

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:18.451
to have the impropriety

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:20.820
that was hinted at by Trump and his team

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:21.921
to be distanced

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:22.922
from the attorney general,

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:23.589
Merrick Garland,

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.224
so that no more thing to keep in mind

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.793
here is the power dynamic.

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:28.761
And as Evan rightly pointed out,

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:29.862
there's a little bit of kudos

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:30.797
that ought to be given

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:32.365
to the entire process here,

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:33.900
because grand juries

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.401
are supposed to be secret.

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:36.469
We're supposed to be

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:38.471
a little bit in the dark here, John.

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:39.505
We're supposed to be wondering

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:41.774
because that presents more fairness

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:44.677
for the defendant or a potential target.

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:46.212
If we know everything

00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:47.880
and the court of public opinion

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.148
can undermine the ability

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:50.416
to get a fair trial,

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:51.784
a fair jury impaneled,

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:54.020
if that were ever to get there,

00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:56.823
based on everything that we do know

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:57.990
and as you correctly, note,

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:00.159
that's limited what we know.

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:02.729
Where do you see things right now?

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:06.099
Well, this

00:06:06.099 --> 00:06:06.733
is, first

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:08.201
of all,
when you're talking about the attorneys

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:09.435
wanting to come in.

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:11.137
We have the reporting from last week,

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:11.671
our excellent

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:13.473
reporting from our own colleagues

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:15.274
about the nature of documents

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:16.676
that may have been viewed,

00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:18.111
whether they were disclosed

00:06:18.111 --> 00:06:20.246
or wanting to be disclosed to anyone.

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:21.581
The idea of his own statements

00:06:21.581 --> 00:06:23.683
before our town hall with Kaitlan Collins

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:24.784
on his intention

00:06:24.784 --> 00:06:26.352
to retain documents and believing

00:06:26.352 --> 00:06:27.887
he had every right to do so.

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:29.021
And then the report

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:30.690
reports of tapes potentially

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:31.023
that show

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:32.291
that he did not believe

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:33.259
that he had the ability

00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:35.428
to show them whenever he wanted to.

00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:36.763
We're waiting on all the culmination

00:06:36.763 --> 00:06:37.764
of that reporting

00:06:37.764 --> 00:06:39.899
based on that, the length of time

00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:40.633
and, of course,

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:41.300
the January

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.802
six prosecution, which, of course, is

00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:44.470
part of what Jack Smith is looking at.

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:46.139
We are really nearing towards

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:48.207
the end of an investigation cycle.

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:50.543
Keep in mind, as though as well as this,

00:06:50.543 --> 00:06:51.277
we are,

00:06:51.277 --> 00:06:51.677
you know,

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:53.312
over 500 days away

00:06:53.312 --> 00:06:55.148
from the presidential election.

00:06:55.148 --> 00:06:56.115
But internally,

00:06:56.115 --> 00:06:57.650
the Department of Justice

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:00.753
has its eyes on the novelty of this

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:02.555
entire investigation

00:07:02.555 --> 00:07:04.290
against a former president

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:04.891
and one who

00:07:04.891 --> 00:07:07.326
wants to have the RNC nomination, again,

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:08.895
a purported frontrunner

00:07:08.895 --> 00:07:09.962
in that very race.

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:11.364
And so they already know

00:07:11.364 --> 00:07:12.565
there are time constraints.

00:07:12.565 --> 00:07:13.466
And when they can

00:07:13.466 --> 00:07:14.934
launch investigations,

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:16.569
launch prosecutions,

00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:18.771
because they do not want to be seen

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:21.374
as interfering with an election.

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:23.643
And so the timeline is already

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:25.745
a little bit strong for that very reason.

00:07:25.745 --> 00:07:27.113
But I suspect, given the fact

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:28.581
that they have all this information

00:07:28.581 --> 00:07:30.416
and if intent was all

00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:31.651
they were waiting for,

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:33.019
the reporting has come in

00:07:33.019 --> 00:07:35.221
and seemed to draw a very clear line

00:07:35.388 --> 00:07:37.290
that they know what that is.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:40.026
Laura Coates, such important context.

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:41.894
Thank you for laying all that out

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:42.929
so clearly. For us.

00:07:42.929 --> 00:07:44.297
I appreciate it, Sarah.

00:07:44.297 --> 00:07:45.131
All right.
Thanks, John.

00:07:45.131 --> 00:07:46.766
Kristen Holmes is going to be joining us

00:07:46.766 --> 00:07:48.267
now in Washington, D.C.

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:50.236
She's been following this case

00:07:50.236 --> 00:07:51.437
and obviously talking

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:53.339
with those surrounding Donald Trump.

00:07:53.339 --> 00:07:55.174
Have you heard anything from them since?

00:07:55.174 --> 00:07:57.310
We have found out that they are

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:58.010
their lawyers are

00:07:58.010 --> 00:07:59.312
now meeting with the DOJ.

00:08:00.913 --> 00:08:02.081
Well,
sir, we haven't had an

00:08:02.081 --> 00:08:04.183
official comment from the Trump campaign.

00:08:04.183 --> 00:08:04.650
However, I did

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:05.952
speak to two advisers

00:08:05.952 --> 00:08:07.987
who gave me some background information

00:08:08.187 --> 00:08:09.322
on what exactly

00:08:09.322 --> 00:08:10.256
this is going to look like,

00:08:10.256 --> 00:08:12.124
what exactly they are trying to ask for.

00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:13.392
You heard Evan mention

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:14.894
this idea that they are characterizing

00:08:14.894 --> 00:08:16.996
this as prosecutorial misconduct.

00:08:16.996 --> 00:08:18.297
I am told by one adviser

00:08:18.297 --> 00:08:18.831
that they plan

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:19.365
to provide

00:08:19.365 --> 00:08:21.901
specific examples of overreach now.

00:08:22.101 --> 00:08:22.668
When I asked

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:24.737
what those specific examples were,

00:08:24.871 --> 00:08:25.805
there was no detail

00:08:25.805 --> 00:08:26.372
given there,

00:08:26.372 --> 00:08:27.306
but something to keep in mind

00:08:27.306 --> 00:08:28.107
that they believe

00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:28.574
that they have

00:08:28.574 --> 00:08:30.176
some kind of evidence here.

00:08:30.176 --> 00:08:30.943
The other thing

00:08:30.943 --> 00:08:31.310
that I am

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:32.578
told by another adviser

00:08:32.578 --> 00:08:33.913
that they are planning to argue

00:08:33.913 --> 00:08:35.014
is that the best thing to do

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:37.583
is to close this case before the election

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:38.417
and essentially

00:08:38.417 --> 00:08:38.985
alleging that

00:08:38.985 --> 00:08:40.453
if not, this could lead

00:08:40.453 --> 00:08:42.455
to election interference.

00:08:42.455 --> 00:08:43.756
That is something that we have heard

00:08:43.756 --> 00:08:44.757
from former President Trump.

00:08:44.757 --> 00:08:46.626
And it gives you somewhat of a preview

00:08:46.626 --> 00:08:48.261
into what he might say

00:08:48.261 --> 00:08:50.162
if he loses the primary.

00:08:50.162 --> 00:08:52.365
As I heard from these advisers

00:08:52.365 --> 00:08:53.299
they believe that this

00:08:53.299 --> 00:08:54.834
Republican primary field

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:56.402
will be completely set

00:08:56.402 --> 00:08:57.303
by the end of the week

00:08:57.303 --> 00:08:58.304
or at least almost set

00:08:58.304 --> 00:08:59.772
and that the election has begun.

00:08:59.772 --> 00:09:01.173
And that's something that they plan

00:09:01.173 --> 00:09:02.208
to argue again.

00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:03.543
That this could interfere

00:09:03.543 --> 00:09:04.343
with that election

00:09:04.343 --> 00:09:04.911
and gives you

00:09:04.911 --> 00:09:05.678
a little bit of insight

00:09:05.678 --> 00:09:07.446
into where the brains are right now.

00:09:07.446 --> 00:09:08.981
Yeah, well, as this goes further

00:09:08.981 --> 00:09:09.549
and gets closer

00:09:09.549 --> 00:09:11.551
and closer to the primaries,

00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:13.119
they're going to make that argument.

00:09:13.119 --> 00:09:15.254
But have they given you any indication

00:09:15.254 --> 00:09:17.089
about what exactly

00:09:17.089 --> 00:09:18.858
they are talking to the DOJ about?

00:09:18.858 --> 00:09:20.860
You said just prosecutorial

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:23.496
misconduct, overreach, but any specifics?

00:09:23.496 --> 00:09:24.263
Not even one.

00:09:25.565 --> 00:09:26.933
Not even one specific.

00:09:26.933 --> 00:09:28.200
And I have asked routinely

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:29.168
what exactly

00:09:29.168 --> 00:09:32.071
they believe was prosecutorial misconduct

00:09:32.171 --> 00:09:33.306
as well as details

00:09:33.306 --> 00:09:35.641
into what they are saying was overreach,

00:09:35.741 --> 00:09:37.810
what kind of examples that they have.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:39.478
Again, I have not heard back on

00:09:39.478 --> 00:09:41.047
anything specific

00:09:41.047 --> 00:09:42.181
as to what they believe

00:09:42.181 --> 00:09:44.150
that this overreach was.

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:45.751
Well, I'm sure we're going to hear

00:09:45.751 --> 00:09:47.320
from someone in this case

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:48.120
after this meeting.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.322
We appreciate your time, Kristen

00:09:49.322 --> 00:09:50.323
Holmes, and your reporting.

